# Food in this world grows on fixed spots that regrow on a timer, yet every law so far forgets a spot as soon as its sighting fades, so the agent re-finds food only by luck. A long LARDER memory of where good morsels were seen, multiplied by a RIPENESS clock that is reset whenever the agent stands on or beside the place and climbs slowly back, injects a source that calls the agent back to a patch about when it should have regrown: a trapline over the remembered map, on top of the darkness-weighted frontier and the footprint trail.

channel source
channel solid
channel free
channel thing
channel scent
channel bad
channel here
channel value
channel dark
channel larder
channel ripe
channel injection
channel wave
channel trail

rule track:
  when 1
  set trail = max(here, 0.97 * trail)

rule darkness:
  when 1
  set dark = 0.5 * (1 - free) * (1 - solid) + 0.5 * avg8(dark)

# where good food has been seen: a long memory that outlives the fading sighting
rule remember:
  when 1
  set larder = max(thing * (1 - bad), 0.9998 * larder)

# a remembered place ripens with time since the agent last stood on or beside it
rule ripen:
  when 1
  set ripe = where(max(here, max8(here)) > 0, 0, min(1, ripe + 0.0004))

# food and frontier as before; a ripe remembered patch calls the agent back (a trapline)
rule inject:
  when 1
  set injection = max(where(scent + thing < 0.05, 0, source), thing * (1 - bad), where(scent + thing < 0.05, source, 0) * (0.3 + 2.0 * dark), 0.5 * larder * ripe) / (1 + 0.5 * sum8(solid))

rule plan:
  when 1
  set wave = max(injection, max(0.94 * max4(wave), 0.916214 * max8(wave))) * (1 - solid * (1 - leak))

rule read:
  when 1
  set value = wave * (1 - 0.4 * trail)
